.TH aaltitoad-ls 1 2026-10-18 "version v1.2.1" AALTITOAD

.SH NAME
aaltitoad-ls \- tick tock automata language server for graphedit

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aaltitoad-ls
[\fB\-h\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR]
[\fB\-v\fI level\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
This program is the language server of the NTTA models of graphedit (see tta(7)).

The server speaks the graph language server protocol of graphedit based on JSON\-RPC messages with content
lengths on the standard input and output.

The server reads the models of the project, builds their network as aaltitoad would run it, and reports what keeps
aaltitoad from running it (see \fDIAGNOSTICS\fR).

It also debugs networks (see \fBDEBUGGING\fR) and can answer queries about them (see \fBQUERIES\fR).

This program is not meant to be run by hand.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
show help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
show version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbosity " " \fIlevel
set the verbosity of the log on the standard error to \fIlevel\fR (6 for max verbosity, default 3: warnings).

.SH DEBUGGING
A debug session starts a runtime that stops before its first tick. When a tick can take several sets of edges, those
sets are the choices of the step.
Breakpoints can be placed on locations and edges, with optional conditions and hit counts.
While the runtime is stopped, variables can be changed, instances can be put into other locations and earlier states
can be restored. Instances are named after their scope, e.g. \fBMain.lamp(1)\fR.

The runtime has no tockers: the environment only changes when its variables are changed in the debugger, and clocks and
timers do not advance by themselves. When no edge is enabled, the runtime stops until a variable changes. The arguments
of a debug configuration change how it runs:
.TP
.B policy
how the runtime chooses between the choices of a step: \fBfirst\fR (the default) or \fBrandom\fR.
.TP
.B seed
the seed of the random choices, so that random runs can be repeated.
.TP
.B delay
milliseconds between two steps when the runtime runs (default 0: as fast as possible).
.TP
.B history
how many states can be restored (default 1000).

.SH QUERIES
The server answers safety- and reachability-queries in the computation tree logic (CTL) format as described in verifier(1):
.TP
.BI "E F " p
can a state in which \fIp\fR holds be reached? If it can, the result has a trace to such a state (a witness).
.TP
.BI "A G " p
does \fIp\fR hold in every state that can be reached? If it does not, the result has a trace to a state in which
\fIp\fR does not hold (a counterexample).
.PP
The predicate \fIp\fR is an expression over the variables of the network, or a location id. Private variables are named
after their instance (\fBMain.lamp(1).on\fR). Locations are named \fIinstance\fB@\fIlocation\fR in expressions, by
their nickname or their id, since the dot already names the private variables. For example:
.TP
.BI "\fBE F Main.lamp(1)@on && !button.1\fR"
asks whether the instance \fBMain.lamp(1)\fR can be in its location \fBon\fR while \fBbutton.1\fR is false.

.PP
The queries are answered with the forward reachability search of verifier(1). If found, a trace is provided.

The search runs step by step, so that the server keeps reading messages: a query can be cancelled, and the server
reports how many states it searched. It answers one query at a time. The option \fBmaxStates\fR of a query (default
100000) bounds the search: a query whose answer needs more states is reported as \fIunknown\fR.

.SH EXAMPLES
Edit the models of a project in graphedit, with aaltitoad\-ls as the language server of its NTTA models:
.PP
.RS
AALTITOAD_LANGUAGE_SERVER="aaltitoad\-ls \-\-verbosity 4" graphedit my\-project/
.RE
.PP
Answer the queries of the project on the command line (the exit code is 1 unless all of them hold):
.PP
.RS
AALTITOAD_LANGUAGE_SERVER=aaltitoad\-ls graphedit\-cli \-\-project my\-project/ verify
.RE

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
The server reports the following diagnostic codes. Codes that start with \fBAALTITOAD\-E\fR are errors, codes that start
with \fBAALTITOAD\-W\fR are warnings.
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E001
no template is the main template (\fBis_main\fR).
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E002
several templates are the main template.
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E003
several models have the same name.
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E004
a template does not have exactly one initial and one final location.
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E005
a connection leads into or out of a subcomponent.
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E006
an edge does not arrive at a location (a nail leads nowhere, to several vertices or in a circle).
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E007
aaltitoad cannot parse an expression (a guard, an update, declarations or the arguments of an invocation).
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E008
a template has extern or persistent declarations.
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E009
a subcomponent names a template that does not exist.
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E010
the arguments of a subcomponent do not match the parameters of its template.
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E011
templates instantiate each other in a circle.
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E012
an expression uses a variable that is not declared.
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-E013
aaltitoad cannot build the network for another reason.
.TP
.B AALTITOAD\-W001
a model file that aaltitoad cannot read (e.g. of graphedit 1.x).


